title Wizard keys — Esc steps back, Ctrl+C asks before it quits, Skip is a button
' purpose: what each key means on a page of a multi-page wizard, and why a lone form keeps its old keys
' covers: internal/choiceui/quit_gate.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go (Outcome, Step, leave, quitKey, drawSkip, Form.Skip)
' covers: internal/choiceui/form_model_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/step_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/env_list_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/list_layer_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/checklist_test.go (TestEscOnPageOneAsksWhenTheFormIsAChecklist)
' covers: internal/choiceui/disabled_hover_test.go
' covers: internal/run/disabled_hover_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_hover_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init.go (runInitSteps, stepQuit)
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_steps_test.go
' covers: e2e/init_steps_test.go
'   the decisions, D5 and D10 ........ _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (DECISIONS, W11)
'   sbx's palette and footer ......... _spec/_conventions/tui-design-language.puml (sbx's OWN TUI)
'   the key line these words sit on .. _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   the dialog the question reuses ... _spec/internal/choiceui/confirm-dialogs.puml
'   init's four pages ................ _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml
'   run's two pages .................. _spec/internal/run/run-spec.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS WRONG ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Esc meant three things in `proveo init`: an error on setup, a skip on
' credentials, a clean end on operator. Ctrl+C shared all three. The footer
' said "esc cancel" on every page, which was true on one of them.
' The Executor, D5: "Adopt sbx: esc back, ^c quit". The recommendation was to
' keep shift+tab. D10: "A focusable Skip button". Not chosen: a control-key
' chord; no skip.
' THE sbx PRECEDENTS, OBSERVED on sbx v0.50.0 (`sbx tui`, 2026-11-10):
'   Ctrl+C    opens "Exit — Do you want to exit?" with "No ↵" selected; ←/→
'             move the selection and ↵ follows it; Esc closes it; a second
'             Ctrl+C quits with status 0 and leaves every sandbox untouched
'   create    a stepped wizard: Esc steps back one page and closes only from
'             page 1; its step chip counts pages from the answers given
'             (1/2 becomes 2/3 once "Local" is chosen)
'
' ── WHAT THE WIZARDS DID NOT TAKE FROM sbx ─────────────────────────────────
' sbx's panels, cards and dashboard: proveo has no long-lived screen. Its
' centred dialogs over a dimmed dashboard: proveo's pages are full-screen
' forms and stay so. Its per-panel key reuse (`r` removes on the left and
' refreshes on the right): one key keeps one meaning across a proveo wizard.
' DECIDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O1): the "no cards" half is REVERSED. The owner
' chose the One Card look after two rounds of mocks. Every wizard page is one
' rounded card: the run and init forms, the scope page and the checks page.
' Every dialog is a card, and the form's open list is a small card. The
' standalone run/attach FilterList is not a card.
' Still not taken: panels, a card per item, a dashboard, a dimmed underlay
' and per-panel key reuse. A page is still full-screen; the card is its
' frame, centred only for a dialog. The reasons above for those still hold.
' The card's geometry: _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (ONE CARD).
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (I3, D4): the quit question now draws over the dimmed
' page, so "a dimmed underlay" is taken for that one dialog. The other
' dialogs run with no page under them and keep the whole screen.
'
' ── EVERY PAGE KEEPS A RENDERING WITH NO TERMINAL ──────────────────────────
' "A form cannot be the only rendering"
' (_spec/_plans/tui-style-deferred-surfaces.puml, surface B).
'   the scope page    not drawn without a TTY, with PROVEO_WIZARD off, with
'                     --print or with --scope; --yes and the scheduler take
'                     the repo root and print `scope: repo root`
'   the run form      skipped unless promptable and not --yes
'   a confirmation    declines unless headed
'   init's pages      each prints one note and returns; the checks print to
'                     the stream, and the result prints either way
' NOT BUILT: a "resolved values" rendering of the run form for a reader with
' no terminal.
'
' ── THE KEYS ON A WIZARD'S PAGE (Step.Of > 1) ──────────────────────────────
'   Enter      forward: Accepted. On the Skip button: Skipped.
'   Esc        Back past page 1. On page 1 it closes the wizard: Cancelled.
'   Ctrl+C, q  a question first; a confirmed answer is Quit.
'   shift+tab  still steps back past page 1. The key line no longer names it.
' The footer reads "esc back" past page 1 and "esc cancel" on it, then
' "ctrl+c quit". Under a narrow screen "ctrl+c quit" drops early: after the
' scroll keys and, on a form with checkboxes, after "space toggle". "enter
' accept" still goes last.
' SINCE 2026-11-13 (owner, O6) THE PAGE COUNT SITS IN THE HEAD. A wizard
' page's title row carries the chip " page n/m ", and "page n/m" leaves the
' key line while the chip draws. The rule for when it does not fit:
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (ONE CARD).
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner: "always display page"): the scope page's
' " scope · n/m " and the checks page's " checks · n/m " are gone. Every
' wizard page names its count with the one word "page", in the chip and on
' the key line.
' ON A CHECKLIST (Form.Checklist; built 2026-11-13, stage 2, unused by init
' until stage 4):
'   Esc        page 1 asks the quit question, as Ctrl+C does (D26); past
'              page 1 it is Back. A list open under the cursor still takes
'              Esc first (ONE LAYER PER KEY). A lone checklist cancels.
'   Enter      Accepted, unless Form.Blocked names a blocker: then nothing.
'   Blocked    a page Form.Blocked names takes Esc, Ctrl+C and q only. The
'              arrows, Tab, Space, typing, "/" and a list's Enter or Esc do
'              nothing: no cursor draws and the key line names none (S2-21).
' The key line says what Enter does: "enter run n steps", "enter next" or
' "enter finish", from Form.EnterWord; Esc reads "esc quit" on page 1. The
' full key line per state: wireframe.puml (THE CHECKLIST CARD).
' NOT BUILT IN STAGE 2: the running state's keys (only Ctrl+C, which stops)
' and a sub-page's "esc later". Both need the stage 3 Session; until then a
' Form with Progress set only draws (Executor, S2-7).
' BUILT IN STAGE 4 (2026-11-13): init's four pages are checklists on one
' Session. While a page runs only Ctrl+C is taken: it cancels the walk's
' context, the step finishes, and init ends stopped there, by SIGINT. A
' sub-page (GitHub access, SSH repair) sets Form.Esc = "later": its key
' line reads "esc later", and Esc there is Back, which init reads as later.
' THE SKIP BUTTON ON A CHECKLIST: pages 3 and 4 keep Skip (owner, Q2 → C),
' so the checklist draws it under its rows at rest, counts its two rows in
' the ladder, and the key line reads "↑↓ row · enter skip · esc …" while
' it is focused. A running page draws no button.
' AMENDED after stage 5's verify (2026-11-13): the ladder counts Skip's two
' rows whenever the form names Skip, and a running page draws them blank
' inside its walls. Counted at rest only, Enter at 80x24 freed them: the
' prose line and the blanks came back, rows moved down 2-3 and the card
' grew from 22 to 24 rows. Pinned by internal/choiceui/session_test.go
' TestARunningPageWithSkipKeepsItsRowsInPlace.
' AMENDED IN STAGE 5 (2026-11-13): page 3 alone keeps Skip, the owner's
' exception to O6 (Q2 → C). Page 4 lost it: Enter with the name field empty
' keeps the name in use, so the button said nothing Enter does not. Form.Skip,
' onSkip, drawSkip and Skipped stay in choiceui for page 3. Page 3 opens on
' its top row with an answer, the first sign-in; StartRow and firstField left
' init (O8). At 80x24 page 3 fits by dropping the blank under the card and
' the prose line (rungs 2 and 3).
'
' ── THE .env FILTER TAKES Enter AND Esc FIRST (owner, O4, 2026-11-13) ──────
' The run form's .env list filters by typing. While its filter is open:
'   /          opens the filter; every printable key after it is text,
'              q j k h l and space included
'   Enter      closes the filter, keeps the matches, and NEVER accepts
'   Esc        clears the query and closes the filter
'   Ctrl+C     still asks first; shift+tab still steps back
' With a query left standing, Esc clears it; the next Esc is the page's.
' SUPERSEDED 2026-11-13 (ONE LAYER PER KEY, below): Esc on a standing query
' closes the list, and the query goes with it. The next Esc is the page's.
' Leaving the cell (←/→, ↑ past the first entry, ↓ past the last, paging)
' drops the query. The key line names the state: "type to narrow · enter
' close · esc clear" while typing, "esc clear" while a query stands.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13: a standing query no longer changes the line. With the
' list open and not typing it reads "↑↓ entry · / filter · enter close · esc
' close" (ONE LAYER PER KEY).
' Precedent: the scope page's Esc already means clear, then cancel
' (_spec/internal/choiceui/scope-tree.puml). The owner chose "Enter closes
' the filter"; "close" is the Executor's word for it (scope says "choose",
' Skip says "skip").
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/env_list_test.go:
'   TestEveryTextKeyIsTextWhileTyping
'   TestEnterClosesTheFilterAndNeverAccepts
'   TestEscClearsTheFilterBeforeItGoesBack
'   TestLeavingTheCellDropsTheFilter
'   TestTheKeyLineWhileTypingNeverOffersAccept
'   TestTheKeyLineWhileTypingAnEmptyQuerySaysEscClear
'
' ── ONE LAYER PER KEY: ENTER AND ESC CLOSE THE INNERMOST MODAL FIRST ───────
' DECIDED 2026-11-13. The owner: "assert the modals showing e.g. the .env
' values take priority for esc/enter (either key closes the modal first)".
' The Executor: Enter and Esc each close ONE layer, innermost first.
'   1 a typing filter   Enter stops typing and keeps the matches; Esc
'                       clears the query and stops typing (O4, unchanged)
'   2 an open list      Enter or Esc closes it; a standing query is dropped
'                       with it
'   3 the form          Enter accepts (or skips on Skip); Esc steps back
'                       past page 1, else cancels (unchanged)
' Every list is a layer: the credentials cells' lists (API keys, OAuth,
' SSH, .env), the ports fold behind ...More, any Row.More or Row.Lists list.
' A list still opens by itself when the cursor reaches its cell.
' A CLOSED LIST STAYS CLOSED while the cursor stays on its cell: ↑↓ move
' rows, and space and tab tick nothing there. It opens again when the
' cursor leaves the cell and comes back (←/→, ↑/↓, paging), or when "/" is
' pressed on a filterable cell, which opens it typing.
' Ctrl+C asks from every layer; shift+tab still steps back; q is text while
' the filter types and asks otherwise.
' THE KEY LINE NAMES THE LAYER. With a list open and not typing it reads
'   [page n/m ·] ↑↓ entry · / filter · enter close · esc close · ctrl+c quit
' "/ filter" only on a filterable list. "enter accept" never shows while a
' list is open. Ranks: _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (E14).
' "space toggle" (rank 2) joins the line on a list that ticks (the ports
' fold), where the owner's line named none; space is the only key that
' ticks a folded port, and the line offered it before this change.
' DIALOGS WERE ALREADY MODAL. formModel, scopeModel and checkModel hand
' every key to the quit gate while it is up, and a confirm dialog runs as
' its own Program. Enter answers the selected button; Esc gives the safe
' one (Stay) and closes only the dialog; the page under it keeps its state.
' The tests below assert that order; no code changed for it.
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/list_layer_test.go:
'   TestEnterClosesAnOpenListAndNeverAccepts
'   TestEscClosesAnOpenListAndNeverGoesBack
'   TestAClosedListOpensAgainWhenTheCursorLeavesItsCellAndReturns
'   TestSlashOpensAClosedFilterableListTyping
'   TestTheKeyLineNamesWhatEnterAndEscCloseOnAList
'   TestEnterAndEscEachCloseOneLayerInnermostFirst
'   TestCtrlCAsksFromEveryLayer
'   TestEnterAndEscReachTheQuitGateBeforeTheFormUnderIt
'   TestEnterAndEscReachTheQuitGateBeforeTheScopePage
'   TestEnterAndEscReachTheQuitGateBeforeTheChecksPage
'   TestEnterAnswersTheSelectedButtonAndEscTheSafeOneInEveryDialog
'
' ── EVERY OPTION TAKES THE CURSOR (DECIDED 2026-11-14) ─────────────────────
' The owner, on `proveo run claudecode`: "let the users hover over API Keys,
' and in the hint say it's not supported. Always let disabled options to be
' hoverable; the hint should explain its status."
' WHAT WAS WRONG. cycle() skipped an Off option on a radio row that was not
' Locked: `if r.Multi || !r.offAt(next)`. The model row's API keys was off
' there, so its OffWhy was text nothing displayed. Checkbox rows and locked
' rows already let the cursor land on any cell.
' THE EXECUTOR'S RULES:
'   1 On every row kind, ←/→, h/l and space (where space moves cells: a
'     radio or locked row) land on every option, a disabled one included.
'     Tab moves no cell; on a checkbox row space ticks, as before.
'   2 On a radio row the cursor is Row.Hover. Landing on an available
'     option chooses it: Selected follows and OnChange fires, as before.
'     Landing on a disabled one sets Row.hoverOff, leaves Selected where it
'     was and fires nothing. Enter accepts the form with the chosen answer,
'     never the hovered one.
'   3 The help names the hovered option and its status; the cells draw the
'     hover in focusOff: wireframe.puml (A DISABLED OPTION TAKES THE CURSOR).
'   4 Selection never returns a disabled option, so the run's decisions do
'     not change. The cursor still opens on the chosen answer: startCursor
'     drops a hover an earlier visit left, and a StartOption that names a
'     disabled option hovers it without choosing it.
'   5 Scope: the run form and init's checklist pages, radio rows included
'     (sbx install's distro package is the one disabled init option today).
'     The scope page and the standalone run> list are out of scope.
' cursorAt reads Hover only while hoverOff holds and Hover is still off. An
' OnChange that frees the hovered option puts the cursor back on the answer,
' and Form.changed then drops hoverOff on that row, so a later OnChange that
' disables the option again leaves the cursor on the answer (verifier pass,
' 2026-11-14; before, the cursor jumped back onto the old hover). No OnChange
' changes a radio row's Off today, and init sets none.
' Leaving the row and coming back keeps the hover, as a checkbox or locked
' row keeps its cursor.
' The key line did not change: "←→ choose" on a form of radio rows, "←→
' move" beside checkbox rows.
' Form.Walk(label, keys...) and Form.RenderOn(label, w, h) are the two
' projections tests outside choiceui read: what each press leaves under the
' cursor (option, help, status lines apart), and the frame with the cursor on
' that row. Form.Render still opens on the answer.
' GOLDENS: the start state is unchanged (MEASURED 2026-11-14:
' internal/choiceui/testdata, cmd/proveo/testdata/init). The verifier pass
' moved six .env fixture frames for the help the locked row gained:
' wireframe.puml (AN OPEN LIST ON A LOCKED ROW, COST).
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/disabled_hover_test.go:
'   TestEveryMoveKeyLandsOnEveryOptionOfEveryRowKind
'   TestARadioRowHoversADisabledOptionAndEnterKeepsTheAnswer
'   TestTheCursorOpensOnTheAnswerAndNeverChoosesADisabledStart
'   TestHoveringADisabledOptionChangesNoAnswer
'   TestAHoverFreedByOnChangeStaysOnTheAnswer
' Pinned by internal/run/disabled_hover_test.go:
'   TestEveryDisabledRunOptionTakesTheCursorAndStatesItsStatus: claudecode,
'   codex, cursor, hermes and opencode; no key, a provider key, the plan key
'   and both; egress readable and not (40 forms). Each form's credentials row
'   holds the inventory promptChoices builds (inventoryOf over those keys, an
'   SSH key, a two-name .env), so its cells open their lists; the test fails
'   when no hover lands on a list entry. Every disabled hover must name
'   itself or its list entry ("› …") and state a status. Until the verifier
'   pass it read an empty inventory and never opened a list.
'   TestClaudecodeHoversAPIKeysWithNoProviderKey
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/init_hover_test.go:
'   TestEveryDisabledInitOptionTakesTheCursorAndStatesItsStatus (the ten
'   golden pages, plus page 1 on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64)
'   TestHoveringDistroPackageSaysWhyItIsOff
' Updated by internal/choiceui/choiceui_test.go: TestGatedOptionRendersItsReason
' asserted the skip; it now asserts the hover.
'
' ── A LONE FORM KEEPS ITS KEYS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' A form with a zero Step is not a wizard: Esc, Ctrl+C and q cancel at once,
' and the footer carries no "ctrl+c quit". That covers the run form when no
' scope page precedes it, and the two GitHub-access forms inside init's
' setup.
' WHY: "Quit" on a nested form would promise to end init, and the code that
' opens those forms returns to the page that asked. A confirm that then only
' cancels one form would lie about what it does.
'
' ── THE QUESTION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' quitGate (quit_gate.go) holds a dialog inside the page's own model, so no
' second Program opens. Its buttons are Stay and Quit. Stay is selected.
'   Enter, Esc          Stay: the page comes back as it was
'   q, or an arrow      selects Quit; Enter then quits (two keys, as D7 asks)
'   Ctrl+C again        Quit: Ctrl+C twice leaves, as teardown does (D2)
' THE WIZARD WORDS ITS OWN QUESTION. Step.Leave carries a title and a body
' (one line per "\n"); every page of the wizard carries the same Step value,
' so the scope page, the form and the checks page all ask in those words.
'   proveo run      "Leave proveo run?" / "No sandbox has been created or
'                   resumed." (internal/run runLeave). Both run pages come
'                   before any sandbox exists, so that is all there is to say.
'   proveo init     the zero Leave, so the generic question: "leave the
'                   wizard?" / "Answers on this page are not saved." / "What
'                   an earlier page did stays done." Init's earlier pages do
'                   run steps, so the second sentence is true there.
' DECIDED 2026-11-11 (user, on the generic question inside `proveo run`:
' "this is too vague to show up in a `proveo run`. Title: Leave proveo run?
' Description: No sandbox has been created or resumed"). The buttons, the
' keys and the key line did not change.
' [Inference] init could word its own question the same way ("Leave proveo
' init?"); nobody asked, so it keeps the generic one.
' The dialog's own tea.Quit command is dropped: the gate reads the answer and
' the page decides.
' SINCE 2026-11-13 the question draws over the dimmed page, not in place of
' it: confirm-dialogs.puml (THE QUIT DIALOG DRAWS OVER THE DIMMED FORM).
' ON A TERMINAL TOO SMALL TO DRAW THE PAGE, Ctrl+C quits at once. A question
' nobody can read would trap the operator.
' The gate's method is named Update because a contract test lets a Bubble Tea
' message reach only a call of that name (tui-stack.puml).
'
' ── SKIP IS A BUTTON, NOT A KEY (D10) ──────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED before the decision: `s` types into the focused field. The
' credentials page opens on a field and the operator page is one field.
' Form.Skip names a button drawn under the rows: "[ Skip ]". Down from the
' last row focuses it; Up, Home or PgUp leaves it. Focused, it is filled and
' carries the enter mark, no row shows the cursor, the help slot is empty,
' and the footer reads "enter skip" in place of "enter accept".
' While it is focused the arrows, space and typing change no answer.
' The button costs two rows (itself and a blank); the layout budget and the
' floor count them.
' "enter accept" STAYS THE E2E ANCHOR. A page opens with the cursor on a row,
' so the words are there when a helper waits for them.
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (owner, O4): a second state drops it. While the .env
' filter is typing the Enter segment reads "enter close", because Enter
' there closes the filter and accepts nothing. The anchor still holds: no
' page opens with a filter typing, and a standing query keeps "enter accept".
' AMENDED 2026-11-13 (ONE LAYER PER KEY): any open list drops it too, a
' standing query included; Enter there reads "enter close". The anchor
' still holds: the run form opens on model, or on trust repo without one
' (TestTheRunFormAsksItsQuestionsInOrder), and neither row carries a list.
' SINCE 2026-11-13 (owner, O8) the run form opens on its top row with an
' answer to change, not on devices; e2e walks that started on devices now
' walk Down from model (choice-prompt-render.puml, WHERE THE CURSOR MAY REST).
'
' ── WHAT EACH CALLER DOES WITH THE OUTCOME ─────────────────────────────────
' SINCE STAGE 4 (2026-11-13) init's four pages, on one Session:
'   init sbx (1/4)          Accepted runs the page; Quit (Esc or Ctrl+C,
'                           confirmed) ends init; on a blocked page every
'                           way off ends with the blocker.
'   init git, shell (2/4)   Accepted runs the page; Back; Quit.
'   init credentials (3/4)  Back; Skipped moves on, stores nothing, and the
'                           result says what sbx holds; Quit.
'   init operator (4/4)     Accepted saves the name, or keeps it when the
'                           field is empty, and closes the card; Back; Quit.
'                           Skip left it in stage 5.
'   init sub-page (2/4)     Accepted saves; Back is later; Quit ends init.
'   init, on Quit           "quit at page n/4", exit 1. No later page runs.
'                           "cancelled at the init prompt" is gone.
' BEFORE STAGE 4:
'   init setup (1/3)        anything but Accepted: "cancelled at the init
'                           prompt", exit 1. Nothing ran yet.
'   init credentials (2/3)  Back; Skipped moves on and stores nothing; Quit.
'   init operator (3/3)     Back; Skipped ends init with the name unchanged;
'                           Quit.
'   init, on Quit           "quit at page n/3 — what earlier pages did stays
'                           done", exit 1. No later page runs.
'   run form (2/2)          Back returns to the scope page; Quit is "quit at
'                           the choice prompt", exit 1.
'   run scope page (1/2)    Esc and a confirmed Ctrl+C both end the run with
'                           "cancelled at the scope prompt".
' EXIT 1, NOT 130 AND NOT 0. Every other prompt the operator closes ends 1
' ("cancelled at …"). Before this change Ctrl+C on init's later pages ended 0,
' as a skip; a shell chain `proveo init && …` then ran on.
' [Inference] 130 would also be defensible: the operator pressed Ctrl+C. No
' signal was delivered, so the status of a refused prompt was kept.
'
' ── WHAT RAN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' macOS and linux/arm64, on tmux against the stub sbx: Esc returns from page
' 2 to page 1 and from 3 to 2; the Skip button moves 2 to 3 and ends 3;
' Ctrl+C asks, Enter stays, and a second Ctrl+C ends init with "quit at page
' 3/3" and status 1. The six older init tests pass through the changed
' helpers. macOS only: the run form steps back with Esc and quits on Ctrl+C
' twice (the container has no sbx).
' The golden frames changed in 14 files, on the key line only.
'
